# Exclude local desktop build artifacts and sidecar binaries from deployments
# These files are large and not needed by the Vercel-hosted frontend/API

# Tauri build outputs
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/bundle/

# Sidecar and bundled node binaries
src-tauri/sidecar/
src-tauri/**/node

# macOS disk images and app bundles
**/*.dmg
**/*.app

# Rust/Cargo build artifacts (safety)
target/

# Common local artifacts
.DS_Store

# Never deploy api test files: every non-underscore file under api/ becomes a
# live serverless function, and a deployed *.test.mjs executes its whole
# node:test suite (production env + Sentry) on every request (WORLDMONITOR-VD).
# Guarded by tests/deploy-config.test.mjs.
api/**/*.test.mjs

# ------ Ivix World Monitor curation (Hobby plan: 12 Serverless Functions max) ------
# Keeping only: market, news, economic, trade, resilience, conflict, sanctions,
# supply-chain (v1), bootstrap.js, rss-proxy.js. That's 10 functions, 2 of
# headroom before the Hobby cap.
#
# api/mcp/ is EXCLUDED ENTIRELY (47 files -> 47 functions would blow the cap).
# scripts/docs-stats.mjs, scripts/generate-public-product-facts.mjs, and
# scripts/generate-inventory-facts.mjs are patched (see their WORLDMONITOR-VD3
# comments) to treat a missing api/mcp/ tree as "tool catalog is empty by
# design" instead of crashing -- that patch is what makes this exclusion safe.
#
# api/health/ (the full domain) and api/health.js (the loose data file docs-
# stats.mjs reads directly) are BOTH excluded -- health was never one of our
# 8 curated domains; only api/health.js needed a one-time carve-out earlier
# and that carve-out is obsolete now that api/mcp/ absence is handled the
# same way health.js's dependents already tolerate.
#
# api/[...notfound].ts and api/not-found.ts are excluded together (the first
# imports the second; excluding only one breaks the build -- WORLDMONITOR-VD2).

